PROJECT: COMPLETE COMPANY ERP MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, ERP consultant, UI/UX designer, database architect, and cybersecurity engineer.

Build a complete, production-oriented ERP Management System for a company. The system must centralize and manage all essential business operations, including customers, leads, sales, employees, departments, inventory, suppliers, purchasing, finance, expenses, invoices, projects, documents, and business analytics.

The system must be modular, scalable, secure, maintainable, and easy to use.

Core requirement: Use Google Sheets as the primary database, accessed through the Google Sheets API using a Google Cloud service account. The frontend must never access Google Sheets directly or expose the service account credentials.

Do not create only a static dashboard or UI prototype. Implement working modules, database operations, authentication, validation, search, filtering, reporting, and integrations.

If a real Google Cloud configuration is not available during development, provide a clearly identified demo mode and an easy configuration process for switching to the real database.

