Data integrity requirements

- Validate all incoming records.
- Check for duplicate records.
- Validate foreign-key references in the application layer.
- Prevent invalid status transitions.
- Use batch reads and writes where possible.
- Minimize unnecessary Google Sheets API requests.
- Support pagination, filtering, sorting, and search at the API level.
- Escape and sanitize user-supplied data.
- Treat all spreadsheet values as untrusted input.
- Prevent formula injection when writing user-controlled values.
- Maintain an audit trail for sensitive changes.
- Implement concurrency controls and conflict detection for important writes.
- Avoid assuming that Google Sheets supports relational transactions or database-level constraints.

For financial records, stock movements, and invoice issuance, use a carefully designed write workflow, validation checks, unique operation IDs, and reconciliation procedures.

Document the limitations of Google Sheets for concurrent writes, transaction processing, and large-scale workloads. Design a repository abstraction so the database can later be migrated to PostgreSQL without rewriting the entire application.

